# FPX payments

Learn about FPX, a common payment method in Malaysia.

Financial Process Exchange (FPX) is a Malaysia-based payment method that allows customers to pay online using their bank credentials. PayNet operates FPX in partnership with participating Malaysian financial institutions.
Payment method family: Bank redirects
Usability: Single-use
Access type: Instant provisional access
Payment confirmation timing: Immediate
Settlement timing: Up to 5 business days (T+5)
Pricing: https://stripe.com/en-my/pricing/local-payment-methods#fpx
## Eligibility and availability 

### Account eligibility
Business location: MY
Account type: ✓ Merchant, ✓ Platform or marketplace (Connect)
Business model: ✓ B2B, ✓ B2C
To process FPX payments and receive payouts, businesses must provide their Business Registration Number (BRN).

Your account might be reviewed after activation to confirm eligibility. While FPX doesn’t enforce any additional website requirements, make sure that you provide a website that meets the [Stripe account activation requirements](https://support.stripe.com/questions/business-website-for-account-activation-faq). You can contact [Stripe support](https://support.stripe.com/) to appeal any FPX capability restrictions.

This payment method doesn’t have any MCC requirements.

Stripe accounts in the following countries can accept FPX payments that settle in a supported currency.

APAC: MY

Customers in the following countries can use FPX.

APAC: MY

### Payment support
Customer location: MY
Presentment currency: MYR
Geographic coverage: ✓ Domestic, ✗ Crossborder
Transaction limits: Minimum amount: 1.00 MYR (B2C), 2.00 MYR (B2B); Maximum amount: 30,000.00 MYR (B2C), 1,000,000.00 MYR (B2B)
