### Mobile Payment Sheet 

FPX supports iOS and Android Payment Sheet for B2C transactions only.

### Sample integration 

View the FPX [sample on GitHub](https://github.com/stripe-samples/accept-a-payment).

## Customer experience 

#### 1. Select FPX

The customer selects FPX and chooses their bank on the merchant's payment page.

#### 2. Go to online banking

The customer is redirected in their browser to their bank's authorization surface. On mobile, FPX might redirect the customer to their banking app.

#### 3. Authorize the payment

The customer signs in and completes their bank's authorization process, which varies by bank.

#### 4. Return to the merchant

After authorization, the customer automatically returns to the merchant's page.

#### 5. Complete the payment

A B2C payment immediately displays as successful. A B2B payment initially displays as pending while confirmation is processed asynchronously, then displays as successful after confirmation.

### Statement descriptors 

When a customer pays with FPX, their bank statement displays the FPX seller ID, seller description (the business name), and seller order number.

Set `statement_descriptor` to control the seller order number for an individual payment. If you don’t provide a payment-level descriptor, Stripe uses the account-level statement descriptor. The `statement_descriptor_suffix` parameter applies only to card payments.

For Connect destination charges without `on_behalf_of`, Stripe uses the platform’s statement descriptor. For direct charges and charges that use `on_behalf_of`, Stripe uses the connected account’s statement descriptor. Learn more about [statement descriptors with Connect](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/statement-descriptors.md).

To reconcile an FPX payment with PayNet records, retrieve the PaymentIntent with `latest_charge` expanded and read `latest_charge.payment_method_details.fpx.transaction_id`.

## Enable FPX 

If you use Stripe front-end products, enable FPX in your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods). Stripe automatically determines which payment methods are most relevant to each customer.

If your integration lists payment methods manually, learn how to [configure FPX as a payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/fpx/accept-a-payment.md).
